Package: ripr
Title: Reverse Information Projection onto Finite Unions of Convex Sets
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Floyd", "Everest", , "me@floydeverest.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Approximates the growth-rate optimal e-variable for a composite
    null hypothesis, in the sense of Grünwald, de Heide and Koolen (2024)
    <doi:10.1093/jrsssb/qkae011>, by computing the reverse information
    projection (RIPr) of a fixed alternative onto a null given by a finite
    union of convex subsets of the parameter space. The subsets may overlap and
    their union may not be convex, so the projection is found by a Frank-Wolfe
    and EM hybrid over mixing measures supported on the individual convex sets.
    The optimiser returns a mixing measure and its induced mixture that
    approximates the RIPr, and makes no claim about validity. Nevertheless,
    an e-variable can be built by deriving a certified upper bound on the
    worst-case null expectation. The observation model, null geometry, and
    quadrature rules are pluggable, with expectations under the alternative
    taken by exact enumeration, deterministic quadrature, or Monte Carlo through
    a common interface.
